:: Upper_Lake_Mist_Start [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.50]
The last private bus down to the Kandy clock tower rumbled away twenty minutes ago, leaving the switchbacks of Upper Lake Road in a wet, chalky silence. Below the stone parapet, the black water of the Bogambara lake lies motionless under a ceiling of hill-country fog.

To your left, the moss-slick retaining wall holds back the giant bamboo thickets of Udawattakele Sanctuary. Your wristwatch reads 11:46 PM—the threshold of the Maddhama midnight watch. Around your right pulse, the three-knotted white Pirith Nula thread blessed at the Dalada Maligawa feels cold and sodden against your skin. Thirty yards down the slope, the single municipal streetlamp sputters with {mutate: "a dying orange sodium vapor tube" -> "the sputtering tallow wick of a cemetery lantern" @2600}.

[[Walk briskly down the middle of the wet asphalt through the bamboo arch->False_Tuk_Headlight][$taboo_walked_samayam = true, $tanikama += 10]]
[[Step beneath the rusted tin awning of the shuttered wayside kadé to wait->Three_Wheeler_Wait][$taboo_walked_samayam = true, $tanikama += 15]]


:: Three_Wheeler_Wait [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.56]
You press your back against the padlocked timber shutters of the tea stall. Not a single three-wheeler engine echoes across the valley. The only sound in the mist is rainwater gurgling down the storm culvert across the lane and the hollow, skeletal knock of giant bamboo culms grinding together overhead.

Then, from twenty paces up the blind curve you just walked down, a woman's voice calls softly through the drizzle—speaking {mutate: "a name muffled by the dripping leaves" -> "the private childhood pet-name only your mother uses when you are sick with fever" @2300}.

[[Turn toward the blind curve and call out to ask who is in the dark->Culvert_Whisper_Echo][$taboo_answered_call = true, $balma += 20]]
[[Clamp your teeth shut, press your thumb to your Pirith Nula, and walk downhill->False_Tuk_Headlight][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Culvert_Whisper_Echo [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.68 #balma:10]
The instant your voice leaves your throat, you realize your mistake: the wet hillside did not echo your words back. Instead, the second syllable of your call is repeated from directly beneath the soles of your shoes inside the stone storm drain.

Dark runoff water sloshes against the rusted iron grate at your feet. Five pale fingers coated in sticky white tree-sap slide upward between the bars, and a wet mouth whispers from the dark pipe: {mutate: "I dropped my baby's shawl into the water, malli" -> "You answered my call in the midnight watch; your tongue is mine now" @2000}.

[[Wrench your heel back from the grate and hurry down the road->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Hold the cold Pirith Nula knot and spit once onto the iron bars->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: False_Tuk_Headlight [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.60]
Behind your left shoulder, a single yellow headlamp beam cuts through the swirling mountain fog. An old black Bajaj three-wheeler coasts slowly down the steep grade—yet its two-stroke engine makes no sound at all, only the wet hiss of bald rubber tires rolling across the tar.

It glides to a halt beside the bamboo retaining wall five paces ahead. Rainwater sheets off the torn black canvas hood. From the pitch-dark passenger bench inside comes the rustle of wet white cotton and {mutate: "the creak of rusted seat springs" -> "a breathless, weeping lullaby hummed to a wet bundle" @2200}.

[[Step off the verge and climb into the backseat out of the rain->Backseat_Wet_Saree][$balma += 20]]
[[Turn away from the silent three-wheeler and climb the mossy forest steps->Sanctuary_Stone_Steps][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Keep your thumb locked on your Pirith Nula and walk past on the far side->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Backseat_Wet_Saree [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.78 #balma:15]
You duck beneath the dripping canvas flap onto the vinyl bench—and the blood drains from your face. The driver's seat in front of you is completely empty. The steering handlebars are rusted solid, tangled in dead Udawattakele creeper vines and dry cobwebs.

Beside your hip, the cushion squelches with freezing water. Sitting pressed tight against your left ribcage in the dark cab is a woman in a soaking white saree, her chin resting almost on your shoulder as she turns her pupil-less eyes toward your cheek: {mutate: "You climbed inside of your own accord, malli" -> "Hold the child while I pin my saree border—my hands are so cold" @1950}.

[[Hurl yourself backward out of the cab onto the wet asphalt->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 15]]
[[Crush your thumb against the Pirith Nula and kick backward onto the road->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]
[[Stay seated on the wet vinyl bench and let her lay the bundle in your lap->Outcome_Athura_Udawattakele_Lullaby][$taboo_accepted_bundle = true, $balma += 45]]


:: Sanctuary_Stone_Steps [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.66]
You scramble up six moss-blackened stone steps toward the padlocked iron gate of the forest sanctuary. Overhead, the gnarled branches of a wild Kaduru tree drip thick, poisonous white latex onto the wet leaves.

When you glance back down at the asphalt lane, the black three-wheeler has vanished—leaving only a waterlogged green banana trunk lying in the tire tracks, while a woman's ragged weeping rises from the hairpin culvert just ahead: {mutate: "it is only the wind whistling through the sanctuary wire" -> "she is waiting at the bend because there is no other road down the mountain" @2200}.

[[Descend the stone steps and approach the hairpin culvert bend->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$tanikama += 5]]


:: Bamboo_Culvert_Approach [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.62]
Where the road hooks sharply above the lake, giant bamboo stalks arch completely across the sky like the ribs of a drowned whale. The mountain air turns abruptly suffocating, thick with the cloying stench of {mutate: "wet roadside Lantana weeds" -> "crushed Kaduru blossoms, camphor water, and sour breast-milk" @2400}.

Sitting barefoot on the low concrete culvert wall in the pouring drizzle is a slender woman draped in an unbleached white saree. Her waist-length black hair hangs in sodden ropes over her face, and she rocks a small white cloth bundle against her collarbone, sobbing as if her ribs are breaking.

[[Cross to the outer gravel verge to slip past without speaking a word->Cross_Road_Verge][$tanikama += 5]]
[[Slow your steps and ask why she is sitting alone in the rain at midnight->Weeping_By_The_Wall][$taboo_answered_call = true, $balma += 15]]


:: Cross_Road_Verge [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.66]
You edge toward the lakeward drop-off, keeping your shoes on the loose wet gravel. Before you can take three silent strides, the sobbing cuts off in mid-breath.

There is no splash of bare feet hitting the asphalt—yet when the streetlamp flickers, she is standing motionless in the exact center of the narrow lane four paces in front of your chest. Her wet white saree pleats hang untidy and unpinned, clinging translucent to her limbs, and from inside the white bundle against her breast comes {mutate: "the sound of rainwater dripping on cloth" -> "the thin, choking wail of a newborn struggling for air" @2200}.

[[Clamp your thumb over your Pirith Nula and lock your eyes on the rain puddle at your feet->Gaze_Down_Puddle][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]
[[Lift your chin to see why she is blocking the downhill road->Look_Into_Her_Eyes][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 25]]


:: Weeping_By_The_Wall [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.68 #balma:10]
At the sound of your voice, her shoulders stop shaking. She rises from the mossy culvert parapet without using her hands. In the sickly amber mist, her skin has the grey, bloodless sheen of peeled manioc root, and there is no hollow philtrum groove above her upper lip.

The white saree border slips loose from her left shoulder as the bundle in her arms writhes and wails louder. She drifts into your path, teeth chattering violently, and breathes: {mutate: "My husband walked down to the lake to find a three-wheeler" -> "You walked alone in Tanikama, and you spoke to me across the water" @2300}.

[[Press your thumb hard against the Pirith Nula and drop your gaze to the puddle->Gaze_Down_Puddle][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]
[[Look straight into her dark eyes to see if she is feverish->Look_Into_Her_Eyes][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 25]]


:: Look_Into_Her_Eyes [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.78 #balma:15]
You raise your eyes to hers—and your breath catches in your windpipe. Her pupils are dilated across the entire iris, two wells of wet pitch that swallow the streetlamp glow without reflecting a single pinpoint of light. A narcotic, suffocating warmth floods behind your temples, making the freezing rain feel like warm bathwater.

Slowly, she lifts her left hand and draws three dripping strands of black hair back across her temple, her long fingers curling inward in a rhythmic, hypnotic gesture. Down at your side, your own right arm {mutate: "hangs numb in the rain" -> "lifts against your will to mirror her exact motion across your forehead" @2000}.

[[Let your hand rise to brush the wet hair from your own forehead->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$taboo_mirrored_gesture = true, $balma += 20, $tanikama += 10]]
[[Grind your thumbnail into the Pirith Nula thread to break the motor mimicry->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Gaze_Down_Puddle [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.52]
You keep your chin pinned to your collarbone and your thumb crushed against the three blessed knots on your wrist. Between your shoes and hers, a black rainwater puddle mirrors the sodium streetlamp.

Floating on the oily film of the puddle are three bruised white Kaduru blossoms. At the upper rim of the water, the sodden white border of her saree sways inches above the stone—and in the reflection beneath the hem, {mutate: "her heels are hidden by the dark mud" -> "there are no ankles or feet at all, only empty air three inches above the tar" @2100}.

[[Edge sideways toward the downhill slope without raising your eyes from the water->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$tanikama -= 5]]
[[Jerk your head up to see how she is suspended above the road->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 20]]


:: The_Slipping_Saree_Plea [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.80]
She glides half a pace closer until her freezing breath fogs your collar. The stench of wet burial cloth, bitter white Kaduru latex, and curdled milk coats your tongue.

The unpinned white saree pleat slips further down her bare shoulder. With a ragged, heartbreaking sob, she thrusts the squirming, crying bundle straight toward your chest with both hands: {mutate: "Ane malli, hold my baby for one heartbeat while I tie my saree pleat" -> "Open your forearms and take the dead weight of my warrant into your blood" @2100}.

[[Open your arms and take the crying infant bundle from her hands->The_Infant_Drop_Trap][$taboo_accepted_bundle = true, $balma += 30]]
[[Lock your elbows against your ribs and step backward down the incline->The_Infant_Drop_Trap][$balma += 5]]


:: The_Infant_Drop_Trap [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.88 #balma:15]
As you recoil half a step, her long waxen fingers suddenly splay wide open. She drops the crying bundle in mid-air.

The white shroud plummets straight toward the jagged granite edge of the culvert drain. Every human instinct in your nervous system screams at you to lunge forward and catch the child—yet in the strobe of the streetlamp, the cloth parts for a millisecond to reveal {mutate: "a tiny, shivering newborn skull" -> "a hacked, sap-bleeding green banana trunk swarming with black ants" @1850}. If you unhook your thumb from the Pirith Nula to catch it, your life is forfeit.

[[Crush the Pirith Nula under your thumb, shut your eyes, and let the bundle strike the stone->Outcome_Athura_Road_Escaped][@anchor_held $balma -= 30]]
[[Lunge forward with both arms to catch the falling child before it hits the rock->Outcome_Athura_Mohini_Bound][$taboo_accepted_bundle = true, $balma += 40]]
[[Mirror her weeping gesture and press both sap-stained hands over your eyes->Outcome_Athura_Kaduru_Sap_Veins][$taboo_mirrored_gesture = true, $balma += 45]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Road_Escaped [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.35]
You bite the inside of your cheek until it bleeds and keep your thumb locked over the sacred thread. The white bundle hits the granite curb with a wet, fibrous crunch—not infant bone, but a freshly severed chunk of green Kesel Kanda banana stem that splits lengthwise across the puddle.

An ear-splitting shriek like wet silk tearing in the wind echoes up into the giant bamboo of Udawattakele. When the yellow fog-lamps of a 5:30 AM vegetable lorry round the bend from Ampitiya, the asphalt is empty save for the split banana trunk and a scatter of poisonous black Kaduru seeds.

[[Examine the forensic case from the Kattadiya exorcist perspective->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$tanikama = 40]]
[[Walk Upper Lake Road again from 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Mohini_Bound [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.90]
The millisecond the wet white bundle touches your forearms, its weight turns to three hundred pounds of freezing graveyard iron. On your right wrist, the three-stranded Pirith Nula snaps like dry cobweb.

You jerk your chin up—and there is no infant in your arms, and no weeping widow before you, only a twelve-foot skeleton draped in wet grave-cloth laughing down through a curtain of dripping black hair as her curved tusks lock over your shoulder. Municipal sweepers find you at dawn curled rigid in the culvert ditch, burning with a 105-degree fever, your forearms locked in an unbreakable cradle around empty air.

[[Accept the Bulath Hurulla summons and step into the Kattadiya role->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$tanikama = 80]]
[[Return to Upper Lake Road at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.46]
Two nights later, in an old tiled house on the Peradeniya slope, the young man sits propped against the lime-washed wall. Both of his forearms remain locked at a ninety-degree angle as though cradling an invisible infant, and whenever rainwater ticks against the windowpane, his lips part in a vacant smile and he hums toward the dark corridor.

His trembling father kneels and lays the Bulath Hurulla sheaf beside your brass pahana lamp. Asking zero questions of the household, you draw the top betel leaf from the pile and pass its blade before the flame.

[[Hold the Pahana flame behind the betel leaf to read the wayside Lakunu->Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]
[[Kneel by the reed mat to inspect his locked forearms and snapped wrist thread first->Patient_Catatonia_Inspection][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.52]
Backlit by the golden flame, the betel leaf exposes the exact anatomy of the midnight ambush: a clouded apex bruise from walking alone in the Maddhama watch, a twisted left vein where he answered her call in the mist, a central midrib perforation where he met her pupil-less gaze, a milky Kaduru-sap sheen across the right blade from mirrored gesture, and black necrosis rotting the stem where he caught the falling bundle.

The leaf leaves no doubt: {mutate: "the boy is merely in shock from hypothermia by the lake" -> "Mala Mohini has sealed the surrogate child contract in his tendons" @2200}.

[[Examine the patient's physical symptoms and broken Pirith Nula in the room->Patient_Catatonia_Inspection][$balma += 5]]
[[Unpack the Three Ambalangoda Kaduru-Wood Masks and cut a fresh Kesel Kanda stem->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$balma += 10]]


:: Patient_Catatonia_Inspection [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.60]
You kneel on the reed mat beside the boy. Clinging to his right wrist is the frayed cotton stub of a snapped Pirith Nula, crusted with bitter white Kaduru latex. His pupils are blown wide, staring past your ear toward the rain-swept doorway as if a woman in white is still standing on the threshold demanding her child.

When you test his biceps, the muscles are petrified like seasoned ironwood. Force will snap his bones before it unbends his arms—to break a mimetic trance, you must stage the three-part Mohini Paliya ritual drama to externalize the phantom infant and sever it before his eyes.

[[Set up the Three Kaduru Masks and the shrouded banana stem in the courtyard->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$tanikama -= 10]]
[[Return to the brass pahana to re-verify the betel leaf veins->Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.58]
Under a temporary gokkola palm awning in the rain-slick courtyard, the yak bera drum begins its hypnotic, rolling pulse. Before the torchlit altar stand three carved Ambalangoda masks of light Kaduru wood alongside a four-foot green banana trunk—the Kesel Kanda—swaddled in white burial cloth like a newborn.

You must dance the three faces of the illusion in strict order: first the alluring Malwathu Coquette mask to capture the boy's catatonic gaze; second the swollen Gabbara Pregnancy mask, groaning under the demon's false burden; and third the Daru Severance mask—where her weeping eyes snap open to resist your forged iron Ketta cleaver as you slice the surrogate bundle in half.

[[Don the three Kaduru masks in sequence and overpower her grip to cleave the Kesel Kanda->Midnight_Kesel_Kanda_Severance][$balma += 10]]


:: Midnight_Kesel_Kanda_Severance [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.84 #balma:15]
Powdered dummala resin explodes into a sheet of blinding gold against the mountain fog. As your Ketta blade bites into the white cloth swaddling the banana trunk at the patient's feet, the brass pahana flame flattens and turns corpse-blue.

From the wet bamboo grove beyond the wall, Mohini's weeping voice shrieks over the thunder of the drum: {mutate: "Do not cut the child in two—he promised to carry it for me!" -> "By the fiery anklet of Goddess Pattini and the Triple Gem, the false contract is severed!" @2000}. Lock the cold iron ward under your thumb and strike every syllable of the Pattini Varama cadence!

[[Hold the sacred ward, chant the Pattini Varama, and cleave the Kesel Kanda in two->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Cured][@anchor_held $balma = 0]]
[[Bring the plantain cleaver down without anchoring the sacred ward->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Failed][$balma += 35]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Cured [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.32]
With the ward locked under your thumb, the heavy iron Ketta shears cleanly through the white shroud and splits the green banana trunk into two halves. Clear, watery plantain sap gushes across the courtyard stones. At that exact instant, the young man's petrified forearms drop limp into his lap with a long, sobbing exhalation as the phantom weight vanishes.

You steep a fresh three-stranded Pirith Nula in turmeric-lime water, chant the protective warrant of Goddess Pattini, and knot it three times around his right wrist as the mist over Kandy Lake turns pale gold with dawn.

[[Replay Casefile 02 from Upper Lake Road at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]
[[Examine a new Bulath Hurulla summons sheaf in Kattadiya Mode->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$balma = 25]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Failed [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.88]
Your thumb slips from the ward as the cleaver descends. Instead of severing the banana trunk, the iron blade skids off the wet stone in a shower of blue sparks, and a freezing gust from the bamboo grove snuffs the dummala torch into black smoke.

On the verandah, the boy's eyes roll back into his skull, his locked forearms tightening around the empty air as the high, wet cry of a newborn infant echoes from inside his own chest.

[[Relight the torch and reset the Three Kaduru Masks->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$balma = 40]]
[[Reach down with bare hands to lift the nicked Kesel Kanda stem from the puddle->Outcome_Kattadiya_Cradle_Contagion][$balma += 35]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Udawattakele_Lullaby [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.92]
The canvas flaps of the three-wheeler seal shut on their own. You never reach the Kandy clock tower, and no search party ever finds your body in the lake.

Weeks later, when late-night three-wheeler drivers round the hairpin culvert on Upper Lake Road in the fog, their headlamps catch {mutate: "an abandoned, rusting chassis by the bamboo wall" -> "two figures waiting in the drizzle—a woman in white, and you sitting beside her holding a rotting banana stem out toward every passing window" @2100}. You belong to the road watch now; no ritual can call you back.

[[Start walking Upper Lake Road again at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 25, $tanikama = 55]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Kaduru_Sap_Veins [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.92]
Because you mirrored her hands during the Maddhama watch, your motor cortex remains permanently wired to hers across the dark.

Before a Kattadiya can even be summoned from the low country, you slip out of the Peradeniya ward during a midnight squall—walking backward up into the giant bamboo thickets of Udawattakele while {mutate: "tears of exhaustion run down your cheeks" -> "thick, poisonous white Kaduru tree-latex weeps from your tear ducts and a woman's voice sobs from your open mouth" @2000}.

[[Start walking Upper Lake Road again at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 25, $tanikama = 55]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Cradle_Contagion [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.94]
The moment your bare palms touch the nicked green banana trunk on the courtyard stones, the fibrous plantain bark turns warm and soft as skin. From the shallow cut where your Ketta blade glanced off, {mutate: "clear plantain water drips onto the mat" -> "hot arterial blood gushes across your wrists and the banana stem wails like a newborn infant" @1950}.

On the verandah, the young man's arms drop free—because your own forearms have petrified at a ninety-degree angle around the screaming bundle, locking the third Kaduru mask permanently to your face.

[[Replay Casefile 02 from Upper Lake Road at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]
[[Re-enter Kattadiya Triage from the beginning->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$balma = 25]]
